{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ונזרעה", :translit "v'nizra'ah", :gloss "and she will be sown / she will produce seed"} {:he "זאת תורת הקנאות", :translit "zot torat ha-k'na'ot", :gloss "this is the law of jealousy"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "S'mikhut: the word ונזרעה adjoins the heading זאת תורת הקנאות in the next verse, so the 'seed' it promises is read as righteous children born after vindication."}], :frame {:text "The Sotah ritual is described in the passage introduced by זאת תורת הקנאות (Numbers 5:29). The Mishnah records that if she is innocent she departs and has children, and Rav Yehudah derives from ונזרעה that her former offspring, if any, are beautified (Sotah 26a). Rashi on Numbers 5:28, citing Sotah 26a, transmits the teaching that if she was barren she now conceives, if she had difficult labors they now ease, if she produced dark ones they now become light, and if she had short ones they now grow tall — and she is praisier than before.", :sources ["Numbers 5:28" "Numbers 5:29" "Sotah 26a" "Rashi on Numbers 5:28"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "S'mikhut: the word ונזרעה adjoins the heading זאת תורת הקנאות in the next verse, so the 'seed' it promises is read as righteous children born after vindication.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:27:07.838359224Z", :model "glm-5.2"}